**7.0 Conclusion** 

The comprehensive aggregation of clinical trial data, real-world evidence, and continuous post-marketing pharmacovigilance definitively establishes that glucagon-like peptide-1 receptor agonists (GLP-1 RAs) and dual GIP/GLP-1 receptor agonists represent a transformative, highly efficacious therapeutic class. They are fundamentally indicated for the rigorous management of type 2 diabetes mellitus, chronic weight management, atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease risk reduction, and metabolic dysfunction-associated steatohepatitis.

The integration of robust cardiovascular and renal outcome data confirms that the pharmacological benefits of these agents extend profoundly beyond mere metabolic stabilization, actively reducing all-cause mortality and delaying end-organ deterioration. While the safety profile necessitates ongoing clinical vigilance—particularly regarding severe gastrointestinal tolerability, the rare incidence of non-arteritic anterior ischemic optic neuropathy, and mechanical complications such as perioperative pulmonary aspiration—these risks are predictable, monitorable, and distinctly outweighed by the substantial, life-prolonging clinical benefits.

The recent regulatory removal of psychiatric safety warnings further reinforces a highly favorable, stabilized benefit-risk equilibrium. Consequently, the overall benefit-risk profile for approved GLP-1 RA therapies remains unequivocally positive when prescribed within authorized indications, avoiding unapproved compounded formulations, and under appropriate clinical oversight.
